            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h4><strong>Better Sleep Starts with Better Air</strong></h4><p></p><p>Research shows that maintaining balanced indoor humidity between 40–60% can promote clearer breathing, prevent dry skin, and reduce irritations that often lead to restless nights (MDPI, 2023). </p><p></p><p>According to Dr. Angela Bell, a professional who specializes in sleep: </p><p><em>“I recommend the Blueair Humidifier H35i to my clients looking to improve their sleep environment. This humidifier maintains optimal air moisture, which helps reduce irritation from dry air, allowing for a more restful night. I’ve found it’s especially helpful during drier months when humidity drops, often impacting sleep quality..”</em> </p><p></p><p>The Blueair Humidifier allows precise control over indoor humidity, supporting deep rest and relaxation. Studies published in the journal Sleep confirm that well-humidified environments can enhance sleep onset and efficiency, ensuring a truly restorative night’s rest (Sleep Journal, 1999). </p><p></p><p> </p><h4><strong>The Science of Humidity and Sleep</strong> </h4><p> </p><p>Dry air can do more than cause discomfort — it can affect your overall health and sleep quality. Low humidity dries out the airways, leading to congestion, itchy eyes, or worsening allergies or asthma symptoms. Over time, this can result in fragmented sleep or frequent night-time awakenings. </p><p></p><p>Maintaining healthy humidity levels not only improves sleep quality but also supports respiratory wellness. Research links balanced humidity to fewer respiratory infections and lower inflammation of the airways (PMC, 2023). </p><p> </p><h4><strong>Clean, Comfortable Air for Healthier Sleep</strong> </h4><p> </p><p>What makes the Blueair Humidifier unique is its dual action: maintaining ideal humidity while also purifying the air. Its advanced filtration system reduces airborne particles, allergens, and impurities that can affect sleep quality. This creates a cleaner and healthier sleep environment, ideal for people with sensitivities or allergies. </p><p></p><p>Dr. Bell notes: </p><p><em>“I personally use and often recommend humidifiers like Blueair to my patients, particularly those who suffer from allergies and experience poor-quality sleep.”</em> </p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
